protests along the Las Vegas Strip are  not unusual for those involved in the  valley civil rights movement for decades  it stirs up memories of earlier fights  for justice in the 1960s and 70s  Ruby Duncan was at the forefront of Las  Vegas civil rights activism in 1971  Duncan led 6000 people along a much  smaller Las Vegas trip today she is  proud of the peaceful protest for  justice but she's disheartened that the  protests have to happen in the first  place and outraged by the death of  George Floyd unconcerned a years old  this weekend we have that full interview  with her online over at 8 News now.com
 

